[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-123[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-123/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Promote the canonical rasterizer out of tests/[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]visual-render-promotion[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual-render-promotion: move render_svg_to_png and the bundled fonts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from tests/ace/tui/visual/ into a runtime src/sase module with lazy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resvg/pillow imports, repoint the visual suite at it, and verify goldens[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stay byte-identical.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Externally-triggerable live-app screenshot export[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]live-screenshot-export[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]live-screenshot-export: add the per-window request-dir protocol and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SIGUSR2-triggered, settle-then-export SVG capture to the live TUI, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the tmux launcher injecting SASE_TUI_SCREENSHOT_DIR and printing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dir.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase screenshot local orchestration[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]screenshot-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after visual-render-promotion, live-screenshot-export[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]screenshot-cli: add the top-level command that launches the TUI in tmux [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with fixed geometry, sends keys with regex settle-waits, triggers the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in-app SVG export, rasterizes to PNG, and cleans up the window unless [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]--keep/--window.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remote capture via --host[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]screenshot-remote[dim] · [dim][/dim]after screenshot-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]screenshot-remote: resolve enrolled machine aliases or raw SSH [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]destinations, run the SVG capture leg remotely over SSH with a contract [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]probe and cleanup modeled on sudo/ssh.py, rasterize locally, and report [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the remote sase version.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Flat-note inline embedding in memory reads[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-inline-embeds[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-inline-embeds: make sase memory read/show render ![\\[target]] [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]links of flat notes inline with depth caps, cycle guards, and no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]duplicate reference/children listings, updating docs and the test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]locking old behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Author the TUI memory notes[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-memory-notes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after screenshot-remote, memory-inline-embeds[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-memory-notes: create tui.md and tui_screenshot.md, reparent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui_perf.md under tui.md, link tui_screenshot from lint_and_test.md, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regenerate agent instructions via sase memory init.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-123","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-123.1","reasoning_effort":